  "reasoning": "The facts describe two kinds of criminal conduct. In the first part, the defendant uses counterfeit money to swap with the seller's genuine cash after purchasing cigarettes, effectively taking the seller's money by deception, which the prosecution characterizes as theft (盗窃) with a large amount. In the second part, the defendant directly deceives a shopkeeper by paying with counterfeit money and keeping the goods, which the prosecution labels as fraud (诈骗罪). Therefore the appropriate charges are theft and fraud.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]盗窃;诈骗<eoa>"
